The {{nihongo|'''House of Officers'''|公議院|Kōgiin}} is the upper house of the [[Diet of Okaiken]]. The [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]] is the lower house.

The House of Officers has 251 members, half of whom are elected every three years to fixed six-year terms. All 251 seats are determined by the Direct Party and Representative Voting System, a form of proportional voting that emphasizes party lists over individual constituencies.

The House of Officers is constitutionally the less powerful of the two houses. While it can reject bills passed by the House of Commoners, its rejection can be overridden by a two-thirds majority vote in the lower house. However, unlike the House of Commoners, the House of Officers cannot be dissolved by the Prime Minister. It serves as a body of continuity, often taking over essential government functions during general election periods or times of national crisis.

== Right to vote and candidature ==
* Sanese nationals aged 18 years and older may vote.
* Sanese nationals aged 30 years and older may run for office in the House of Officers (higher than the age of 25 required for the Lower House).

== Differences between the Upper and Lower Houses ==
The House of Commoners (Lower House) possesses several powers not given to the House of Officers (Upper House). 

* Legislative Supremacy: If a bill is passed by the House of Commoners but is voted down or amended by the House of Officers, the House of Commoners can override the decision with a two-thirds majority vote. 
* Treaties and Budget: In the case of international treaties, the national budget, and the designation of the Prime Minister, the decision of the House of Commoners automatically prevails after a mandatory waiting period (usually 30 days), even if the House of Officers dissents.

'''Term Differences:'''
* House of Officers: Members sit for fixed '''six-year terms''', with half the house up for election every three years. The House cannot be dissolved.
* House of Commoners: Members are elected to '''four-year terms''', but the House may be dissolved by the Prime Minister at any time, usually leading to snap elections.

Because of its fixed terms and lack of dissolution, the House of Officers is often described as the "Seat of Reason" ({{nihongo|良識の府|Ryōshiki no fu}}), designed to be less susceptible to momentary populist waves than the Lower House.

== Current composition ==


As of December 2025, the composition reflects the results of the [[Okaiken upper house election, 2025|July 2025 election]].

While the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken|PPO]] lost its majority in the Lower House in the October 2025 general election, it remains the largest party in the Upper House with 105 seats, having performed strongly in the July 2025 cycle before the government's popularity dipped.

The [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|LDP]] forms the largest opposition bloc with 72 seats. The [[Sanese Communist Party|SCP]] retains a significant presence (38 seats) in the Upper House due to members elected in previous cycles (2019 and 2022) who are not yet up for re-election, despite the party's collapse in the Lower House. The [[Okaiken Socialist Party|OSP]], while surging in the Lower House, has a smaller footprint here (13 seats) as the "Nakayama Boom" occurred after the Upper House election cycle.

